Hey, could you set me up a tiny scratch playground so I can show a teammate how Postgres handles JSONB? Please create a fresh schema called agenticmcpe_bench_jsondocs_showcase, and inside it build a table called app_events with an id bigint identity column as the primary key and a payload jsonb column. Then insert exactly four rows with these literal JSON documents:

1. {"event_type":"login","user_id":42,"tags":["web","morning"]}
2. {"event_type":"purchase","user_id":42,"amount":19.99,"tags":["web","book"]}
3. {"event_type":"logout","user_id":7,"tags":["mobile"]}
